# Documentation sync (required)

When you change **application behavior, APIs, schema, roles, routes, or user-facing flows**, you **must** update the matching HCIP docs in the same change. Do not leave docs stale.

## Source of truth map

| If you change… | Update… |
|----------------|---------|
| Product vision / principles / scope | `docs/01-Product-Constitution.md` |
| Actors, domains, entities | `docs/02-Domain-Model.md` |
| App structure, FE/BE layout, deploy | `docs/03-System-Architecture.md` |
| Apply, parse, match, recruiter/Head HR journeys | `docs/04-Workflow.md` |
| Ontology / knowledge (future) | `docs/05-Ontology.md` |
| Parsing, ATS, AI features | `docs/06-AI.md` |
| HTTP routes / blueprints | `docs/07-API.md` (+ run `python scripts/sync_docs_from_code.py`) |
| Tables / migrations / indexes | `docs/08-Database.md` (+ run sync script) |
| Authn/z, RBAC, privacy | `docs/09-Security.md` |
| Phased plans | `docs/10-Roadmap.md` |
| Local setup / env | `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` |
| Doc index / SoT order | `docs/README.md` |

## Rules

1. Label **Current** vs **Future** explicitly. Never document unshipped UI/APIs as current.
2. Prefer editing `docs/01`–`10` — not `docs/legacy/` (archive only).
3. After adding/removing Flask routes or `schema_pg` files, run:
   `python scripts/sync_docs_from_code.py`
4. If a UI control is removed (e.g. save/bookmark), remove it from workflows and note schema scaffolds if tables remain.
5. In the PR/commit summary, mention which doc files were updated (or why none were needed).

## Out of scope for auto-prose

Narrative sections (vision, principles) are human/AI-edited. The sync script only refreshes **generated route/schema inventories** inside `07-API.md` and `08-Database.md`.
